@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Responses request schema
+
+Import `createResponseSchema` from `@xsai-ext/responses/schema` with Valibot 1.4.2 or later.
+The default SDK entrypoint does not load Valibot. The optional peer belongs only to this subpath.
+The schema uses snake_case wire fields and supports JSON and streaming requests.
+It permits provider state, such as `store: true`, response references, and file IDs.
+A shared-account gateway must apply its own policy before forwarding a request.
+
+`openresponses-schema.ts` is generated from the request-reachable schemas of https://www.openresponses.org/openapi/openapi.json (retrieved 2026-09-16).
+The normalized source snapshot is `request-openapi.json`. It removes discriminators as xsai's existing generation config does.
+Array-item unions are lifted into named references because openapi-ts 0.99.0 emits unknown array items for inline unions.
+Generate with `openapi-ts -i request-openapi.json -o generated -p @hey-api/typescript valibot` using openapi-ts 0.99.0 and TypeScript 6.0.3.
+Copy `generated/valibot.gen.ts` to `openresponses-schema.ts`.
+`schema.ts` adds the OpenAI web-search and replay fields already supported by the patched SDK.
+Bundle that entrypoint as ESM with Valibot external to produce `schema.js`.
+The exported TypeScript source retains composable schema types without duplicating generated declarations.
+
+This is the xsai-supported request subset, not a validator for every OpenAI hosted tool.
+References: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/responses/create and https://github.com/openai/openai-python/tree/main/src/openai/types/responses.
+Upstream contribution should add this as a separate schema build entrypoint and retain the request schema generation step.
